.TH CC-INSOMNII 1 "2026-06-23" "cc-insomnii 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cc-insomnii \- bedtime shaming statusline for Claude Code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cc-insomnii
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
echo \fIJSON\fR |
.B cc-insomnii
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cc-insomnii
is a Claude Code statusline plugin that monitors the current time relative to a
configured bedtime and escalates its output through six modes of increasing
urgency as the night wears on.

It reads a JSON payload from stdin (the Claude Code statusline protocol) and
writes a formatted statusline string to stdout. The output uses ANSI escape
codes and is designed to be rendered directly in the Claude Code terminal.

When all is well and it is not yet close to bedtime,
.B cc-insomnii
shows a plain clock glyph with the current time. As bedtime approaches and
passes, the display escalates through warning colors, blinking animations,
rainbow character-chase effects, rotating shame messages, and finally a full
visual chaos mode that will make you question your life choices.

Morning motivation messages are shown between 07:00 and 15:59 when shame is
not active, as a small reward for having survived the night. From the dawn
threshold (default 04:00) until 07:00, when shame is not active, a dim sunrise
glyph and a quiet message are shown instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-after= CMD
Composition mode. Renders the cc-insomnii line FIRST (always the top line),
then feeds the same stdin JSON to
.I CMD
and prints
.IR CMD 's
output verbatim below. Use this to put cc-insomnii ON TOP of an existing
statusline tool instead of replacing it \(em the user keeps every metric
the original renders, with the bedtime nudge as the prominent top line. If
.I CMD
fails or its output is empty, the cc-insomnii line still renders cleanly
(graceful degradation) and
.B cc-insomnii
itself exits 0.
.IP
Quote
.I CMD
when it contains spaces: the inner quotes in
.B \-\-after='ccusage statusline'
keep the whole command together as a single argument. Passing
.B \-\-after
more than once is an error (exit 2).
.IP
Example
.B settings.json
entry:
.RS
.nf
{
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "cc-insomnii --after='ccusage statusline'"
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.IP
The
.B install.sh
helper detects an existing
.B statusLine.command
and prints this snippet for you, marked
.BR RECOMMENDED .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_HOME
Path to the cc-insomnii installation directory. Used to locate
.IR config/shame-messages.json .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_BEDTIME
Bedtime in
.I HH:MM
24-hour format. An evening, night, or after-midnight value (18:00\-05:59) is
supported (see
.BR MODES ).
An invalid value (not
.IR HH:MM ,
or outside 00:00\-23:59) is rejected with a warning on stderr and falls back to
the default so the statusline still renders. Default:
.BR 23:00 .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_DAWN
Dawn threshold in
.I HH:MM
24-hour format, governing two behaviors. While a shame mode is active, being
up past this time forces mode 5 \(em this override applies only for a dawn
before 06:00 (after the 06:00 morning cutoff the night window has already
closed). When no shame mode is active, a dim dawn greeting (see
.BR MODES )
is shown from this time until 07:00, so a dawn from 00:01 to 06:59 still
produces a greeting. A value of 00:00 is treated as unset (neither effect
fires). An invalid value is rejected with a warning on stderr and falls back
to the default. Default:
.BR 04:00 .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_SHAME
Enable or disable shame messages. Set to
.B false
\(em or any of
.BR 0 ", " no ", " off ", " disabled
(any case) \(em to silence them. The
.BR CC_INSOMNII_MOTIVATION ", " CC_INSOMNII_RAINBOW ", and " CC_INSOMNII_BREATHING
toggles accept the same falsy spellings. Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_MOTIVATION
Enable or disable morning motivation messages (07:00\-15:59). Set to
.B false
to disable. Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_RAINBOW
Enable or disable the rainbow character-chase animation on the clock display.
Set to
.B false
for plain bold text. Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_BREATHING
Enable or disable the breathing pulse animation on the glyph; it also cycles the
shame text color in modes 1 and up. Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_COLOR
Color override. A falsy value
.RB ( never ", " false ", " 0 ", " no ", " off ", " disabled )
forces a no-color line: every ANSI escape is dropped, the rainbow chase falls
back to plain text, and the mode-5 char-decay is skipped so the clock stays
legible. A truthy value
.RB ( always ", " force ", " on ", " true )
keeps color on even when
.B NO_COLOR
is set. Unset (auto) keeps the default colored render. cc-insomnii also honors
the
.B NO_COLOR
convention (any non-empty value) and
.BR "TERM=dumb" .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_ASCII
Swap the emoji glyph pools \(em night, doom, sparkle, moon, dawn \(em for 7-bit
ASCII equivalents, for terminals or fonts without emoji support. Color is kept.
A falsy spelling (as above) disables it. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_ACCESSIBLE
Screen-reader / accessible mode. Implies no color and ASCII glyphs, and drops
every animation (blink, reverse, strobe, char-decay, glyph swarm, matrix drip),
leaving a stable
.I time +elapsed message
line in every mode. A falsy spelling disables it. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_MODEL
Show the model name from the statusline payload
.RI ( model.display_name )
as a dim badge in the calm modes (plain, motivation, dawn). The name is printed
verbatim, so any family \(em Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, Fable \(em surfaces without a
code change. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_CONTEXT
Paint a red
.B [!]
marker before the clock, in the shame modes, when the session is deep into its
context window:
.I context_window.used_percentage
at 80 or above, or the legacy
.I exceeds_200k_tokens
flag. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_DURATION
Append the session duration
.RI ( cost.total_duration_ms ,
formatted
.IR Hh Mm )
to the clock in the shame modes. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_COST
In shame modes, append the session dollar cost
.RI ( cost.total_cost_usd ,
as
.IR $X.XX )
to the shame text, and \(em at or above
.B CC_INSOMNII_COST_BUMP
dollars \(em escalate the shame message one tier so an expensive early session
reads as harshly as a much later free one. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_COST_BUMP
Whole-dollar threshold at or above which
.B CC_INSOMNII_COST
bumps the shame message tier. Default:
.BR 5 .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_THEME
Color theme, selecting the whole palette set:
.BR vibe " (default rainbow), " mono " (grayscale), " amber ", " matrix
(green), or
.BR ocean " (blue)."
An unknown value falls back to
.BR vibe .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_PALETTE
With
.BR escalating ,
each shame mode anchors a different region of the active palette so the mode is
legible from color alone;
.B classic
(the default) keeps the single shared 3-second cycle. Default:
.BR classic .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_QUIET
A
.I HH:MM\-HH:MM
window (wrapping past midnight is allowed) in which an active shame mode is
capped at mode 1: the message and elapsed counter remain, but the strobe,
char-decay and glyph swarm are suppressed \(em for users who must stay up. A
malformed value warns on stderr and is ignored. Default: unset.
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_CONFIG
Override path to the user config file. Default:
.IR ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/cc-insomnii/config.json .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_MESSAGES
Override path to the shame messages file. When set, replaces the shipped
.IR config/shame-messages.json .
.TP
.B CC_INSOMNII_NOW
Render as if the wall clock read this
.I HH:MM
time instead of the real one. Lets you preview any mode \(em the approach
sparkle, a shame escalation, the dawn or motivation window \(em without waiting
for that time of day. The epoch used for animation and message rotation is
derived deterministically from the value, so a given preview is reproducible.
Invalid values (not
.IR HH:MM ,
or outside 00:00\-23:59) exit non-zero. Intended for previewing and testing;
unset in normal use.
.SH CONFIGURATION
User configuration is read from
.IR ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/cc-insomnii/config.json .
All keys are optional; missing keys fall back to compiled defaults.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
{
  "bedtime": "23:00",
  "dawn": "04:00",
  "shame": { "enabled": true },
  "motivation": { "enabled": true },
  "rainbow": { "enabled": true },
  "breathing": { "enabled": true }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
See
.I examples/config.json
in the cc-insomnii installation directory for a fully commented reference.
.SH MODES
.B cc-insomnii
shows a plain moon glyph until 30 minutes before bedtime, then escalates through
six modes (0\-5) as bedtime approaches and passes:
.TP
.B Mode 0 \- Approaching
0\-30 minutes before bedtime. A cyan sparkle glyph with an optional breathing
pulse. No shame, no blinking.
.TP
.B Mode 1 \- Bedtime
Bedtime has passed; less than 1 hour overdue. Rainbow character-chase clock with
elapsed time (+Xm), a rotating shame message, and a slow blink.
.TP
.B Mode 2 \- +1h
1\-2 hours past bedtime. Adds an underline to the shame text. Slow blink.
.TP
.B Mode 3 \- +2h
2\-3 hours past bedtime. Adds a matrix-drip prefix and a rapid blink.
.TP
.B Mode 4 \- +3h
3\-4 hours past bedtime. Adds a reverse pulse on odd seconds and a strobe.
Messages are at maximum urgency.
.TP
.B Mode 5 \- Post-dawn
More than 4 hours past bedtime, or \(em while a shame mode is active \(em the
current time is past the dawn threshold (default 04:00, applied between dawn and
the 06:00 morning cutoff). Char-decay clock, a three-glyph swarm, and the doom
glyph set. You are no longer making good decisions.
.PP
The elapsed counter is the shortest signed distance to bedtime on the 24-hour
clock, so it is correct for an evening, night, or after-midnight bedtime
(18:00\-05:59, e.g.
.IR 23:00 ,
.IR 01:00 ):
it counts up from bedtime, wraps across midnight, and the night runs until the
~06:00 morning cutoff, after which the dawn and motivation windows take over. A
daytime bedtime (06:00\-17:59, e.g.
.IR 09:00 ,
.IR 14:00 )
is outside this range \(em the night-window model assumes the night spans the
06:00 cutoff, so the elapsed escalation there is inaccurate. Use an evening or
night bedtime.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${CC_INSOMNII_HOME}/config/shame-messages.json
Shipped shame and motivation message catalog.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/cc-insomnii/config.json
User configuration file.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/cc-insomnii/messages.json
User message override. When present, replaces the shipped message catalog
entirely.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/cc-insomnii
Default symlink location for the binary (or
.I ~/.local/bin/cc-insomnii
for non-root installs).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claudii (1)
